   "target": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"
  },
  "source": "Digital Corpus of Sanskrit (DCS), text ID 89. http://www.sanskrit-linguistics.org/dcs/ Segmentation follows the DCS line/pāda boundaries; chapter and verse labels are taken from the DCS references.",
  "text_id": "89",
  "collection": "DCS"
 },
 "body": [
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "1"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 1"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.1",
      "label": "DCS 1.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāvyaṃ khalu grāhyamupādeyaṃ bhavatyalaṃkārāt ||",
       "translated_text": "Poetry indeed becomes worthy of acceptance and adoption through ornamentation.",
       "segment_number": 360874
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.2",
      "label": "DCS 1.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāvyaśabdo'yaṃ guṇālaṃkārasaṃskṛtayoḥ śabdārthayor vartate ||",
       "translated_text": "The word “poetry” applies to word and meaning refined by qualities and ornaments.",
       "segment_number": 360875
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.3",
      "label": "DCS 1.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "bhaktyā tu śabdārthamātravacano 'tra gṛhyate ||",
       "translated_text": "Here, however, it is understood by secondary usage as denoting merely word and meaning.",
       "segment_number": 360876
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.4",
      "label": "DCS 1.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ko 'sāv alaṃkāra ityata āha ||",
       "translated_text": "What is that ornamentation? In response, he says:",
       "segment_number": 360877
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "2"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 2"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.1",
      "label": "DCS 2.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "alaṃkṛtiralaṃkāraḥ",
       "translated_text": "Adornment is <s>alaṃkāra</s> (ornamentation).",
       "segment_number": 360878
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "karaṇavyutpattyā punaralaṃkāraśabdo yamakādiṣu vartate ||",
       "translated_text": "When derived in the instrumental sense, however, the word <s>alaṃkāra</s> denotes such figures as <s>yamaka</s> (repetition).",
       "segment_number": 360879
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "3"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 3"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.1",
      "label": "DCS 3.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sa khalvalaṃkāro doṣahānād guṇālaṃkārādānācca saṃpādyaḥ kaveḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "That ornamentation must indeed be accomplished by the poet through the removal of faults and the adoption of qualities and ornaments.",
       "segment_number": 360880
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "4"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 4"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_4.1",
      "label": "DCS 4.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "te caite doṣaguṇālaṃkārahānādāne śāstrādeva gantavye ||",
       "translated_text": "These two procedures—the removal of faults and the adoption of qualities and ornaments—can be learned only from the treatise.",
       "segment_number": 360881
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_4.2",
      "label": "DCS 4.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tato jñātvā doṣāñjahyādguṇālaṃkārān ādadīteti ||",
       "translated_text": "Therefore, after recognizing the faults, one should discard them and adopt the qualities and ornaments.",
       "segment_number": 360882
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_4.3",
      "label": "DCS 4.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kaṃ punaralaṃkāravatā kāvyena phalaṃ yenaitadartho'yaṃ yatna ityata āha ||",
       "translated_text": "But what is the fruit of ornamented poetry that makes this effort worthwhile? In response, he says:",
       "segment_number": 360883
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "5"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 5"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.1",
      "label": "DCS 5.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāvyaṃ saccāru dṛṣṭaprayojanaṃ prītihetutvāt ||",
       "translated_text": "Good poetry is beautiful and has a visible purpose, because it causes pleasure.",
       "segment_number": 360884
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.2",
      "label": "DCS 5.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "adṛṣṭaprayojanaṃ kīrtihetutvāt ||",
       "translated_text": "It also has an unseen purpose, because it causes fame.",
       "segment_number": 360885
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.3",
      "label": "DCS 5.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "atra ślokāḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "Here are verses:",
       "segment_number": 360886
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.4",
      "label": "DCS 5.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "pratiṣṭhāṃ kāvyabandhasya yaśasaḥ saraṇiṃ viduḥ",
       "translated_text": "They know it as the foundation of poetic composition and the path to fame,",
       "segment_number": 360887
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "akīrtivartanīṃ tvetāṃ kukavitvaviḍambanām ||",
       "translated_text": "but this travesty of bad poetry as the road to infamy.",
       "segment_number": 360888
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.5",
      "label": "DCS 5.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kīrtiṃ svargaphalāmāhurāsaṃsāraṃ vipaścitaḥ",
       "translated_text": "The wise say that fame, whose fruit is heaven, lasts for as long as the cycle of existence,",
       "segment_number": 360889
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "akīrtiṃ tu nirālokanarakoddeśadūtikām ||",
       "translated_text": "but that infamy is a messenger pointing toward the lightless region of hell.",
       "segment_number": 360890
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_5.6",
      "label": "DCS 5.6"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasmātkīrtimupādātumakīrtiṃ ca vyapohitum",
       "translated_text": "Therefore, to acquire fame and cast off infamy,",
       "segment_number": 360891
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāvyālaṃkāraśāstrārthaḥ prasādyaḥ kavipuṃgavaiḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "the meaning of the treatise on poetic ornament should be mastered by the foremost poets.",
       "segment_number": 360892
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "6"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 6"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_6.1",
      "label": "DCS 6.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "iha khalu dvividhāḥ kavayastiṣṭhanti ||",
       "translated_text": "Now, there are indeed two kinds of poets:",
       "segment_number": 360893
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_6.2",
      "label": "DCS 6.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "arocakinaḥ satṛṇābhyavahāriṇaśceti ||",
       "translated_text": "those without appetite and those who devour everything together with the grass.",
       "segment_number": 360894
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_6.3",
      "label": "DCS 6.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "arocakisatṛṇābhyavahāriśabdau gauṇārthau ||",
       "translated_text": "The expressions “without appetite” and “devouring everything together with the grass” are used figuratively.",
       "segment_number": 360895
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_6.4",
      "label": "DCS 6.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ko'sāvarthaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "What is their intended meaning?",
       "segment_number": 360896
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_6.5",
      "label": "DCS 6.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vivekitvamavivekitvaṃ ceti ||",
       "translated_text": "Discernment and lack of discernment, respectively.",
       "segment_number": 360897
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "7"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 7"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_7.1",
      "label": "DCS 7.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "pūrve khalvarocakinaḥ śiṣyāḥ śāsanīyā vivekitvādvivecanaśīlatvāt ||",
       "translated_text": "The former, those without appetite, are indeed pupils who can be instructed, because they are discerning and habitually discriminate.",
       "segment_number": 360898
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "8"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 8"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_8.1",
      "label": "DCS 8.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "itare satṛṇābhyavahāriṇo na śiṣyāstadviparyayādavivecanaśīlatvāt ||",
       "translated_text": "The others, who devour everything together with the grass, are not pupils, because they are the opposite and habitually fail to discriminate.",
       "segment_number": 360899
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_8.2",
      "label": "DCS 8.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na ca śīlamapākartuṃ śakyam ||",
       "translated_text": "A disposition cannot be removed.",
       "segment_number": 360900
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_8.3",
      "label": "DCS 8.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na caivam ||",
       "translated_text": "Nor is the situation otherwise.",
       "segment_number": 360901
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_8.4",
      "label": "DCS 8.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "śāstraṃ sarvānugrāhi ko vā manyate ||",
       "translated_text": "Who, indeed, thinks that a treatise benefits everyone?",
       "segment_number": 360902
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_8.5",
      "label": "DCS 8.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadāha ||",
       "translated_text": "Thus he says:",
       "segment_number": 360903
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "9"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 9"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_9.1",
      "label": "DCS 9.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na khalu śāstramadravyeṣvavivekiṣvarthavat prayojanavat ||",
       "translated_text": "A treatise is certainly not meaningful or useful for those who are unsuitable material—that is, those without discernment.",
       "segment_number": 360904
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_9.2",
      "label": "DCS 9.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nidarśanamāha ||",
       "translated_text": "He gives an illustration:",
       "segment_number": 360905
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "10"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 10"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_10.1",
      "label": "DCS 10.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na iha katakaṃ payasa iva paṅkasya prasādanāya bhavatīti ||",
       "translated_text": "A <s>kataka</s> nut cannot clarify mud here as it can water.",
       "segment_number": 360906
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_10.2",
      "label": "DCS 10.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "adhikāriṇo nirūpya rītiniścayārthamāha ||",
       "translated_text": "Having identified those qualified to study, he speaks in order to establish the doctrine of style:",
       "segment_number": 360907
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "11"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 11"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_11.1",
      "label": "DCS 11.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "rītirnāmeyamātmā kāvyasya śarīrasyeveti vākyaśeṣaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "This <s>rīti</s> (style), as it is called, is the soul of poetry, just as the soul is that of the body—such is the completion of the sentence.",
       "segment_number": 360908
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_11.2",
      "label": "DCS 11.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kā punariyaṃ rītirityata āha ||",
       "translated_text": "But what is this <s>rīti</s>? In response, he says:",
       "segment_number": 360909
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "12"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 12"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_12.1",
      "label": "DCS 12.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "viśeṣavatī padānāṃ racanā rītiḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "<s>Rīti</s> is an arrangement of words possessing a distinctive quality.",
       "segment_number": 360910
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_12.2",
      "label": "DCS 12.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ko 'sau viśeṣa ityāha ||",
       "translated_text": "What is that distinctive quality? He says:",
       "segment_number": 360911
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "13"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 13"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_13.1",
      "label": "DCS 13.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vakṣyamāṇaguṇasvarūpo viśeṣaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "The distinctive quality consists in the nature of the qualities that will be described.",
       "segment_number": 360912
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "14"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 14"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_14.1",
      "label": "DCS 14.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sā ceyaṃ rītistridhā bhidyate vaidarbhī gauḍīyā pāñcālī ceti ||",
       "translated_text": "This <s>rīti</s> is divided into three: <s>Vaidarbhī</s>, <s>Gauḍīyā</s>, and <s>Pāñcālī</s>.",
       "segment_number": 360913
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_14.2",
      "label": "DCS 14.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kiṃ punardeśavaśāddravyavadguṇotpattiḥ kāvyānāṃ yenāyaṃ deśavyapadeśaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "Do qualities arise in poems under the influence of regions, as qualities arise in substances, so that they receive these regional designations?",
       "segment_number": 360914
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_14.3",
      "label": "DCS 14.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "naivaṃ yadāha ||",
       "translated_text": "It is not so, as he says:",
       "segment_number": 360915
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "15"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 15"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_15.1",
      "label": "DCS 15.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vidarbhagauḍapañcāleṣu deśeṣu tatratyaiḥ kavibhirbahudhā svarūpamupalabdhatvāddeśasamākhyā ||",
       "translated_text": "They are named after regions because poets belonging to the regions of <s>Vidarbha</s>, <s>Gauḍa</s>, and <s>Pañcāla</s> were observed to employ their forms in many ways.",
       "segment_number": 360916
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_15.2",
      "label": "DCS 15.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na punardeśaiḥ kiṃcidupakriyate kāvyānām ||",
       "translated_text": "The regions themselves do not confer anything upon poems.",
       "segment_number": 360917
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_15.3",
      "label": "DCS 15.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tāsāṃ guṇabhedādbhedamāha ||",
       "translated_text": "He states their division according to differences in their qualities:",
       "segment_number": 360918
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "16"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 16"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.1",
      "label": "DCS 16.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "samagrairojaḥprasādaprabhṛtibhirguṇairupetā vaidarbhī nāma rītiriti ||",
       "translated_text": "The style called <s>Vaidarbhī</s> is endowed with all the qualities, beginning with vigor and lucidity.",
       "segment_number": 360919
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.2",
      "label": "DCS 16.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "atra ślokaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "Here is a verse:",
       "segment_number": 360920
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.3",
      "label": "DCS 16.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "aspṛṣṭā doṣamātrābhiḥ samagraguṇagumphitā",
       "translated_text": "Untouched by even the slightest faults and woven together with all the qualities,",
       "segment_number": 360921
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vipañcīsvarasaubhāgyā vaidarbhī rītiriṣyate ||",
       "translated_text": "the <s>Vaidarbhī</s> style, blessed with the beauty of a lute’s tones, is approved.",
       "segment_number": 360922
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.4",
      "label": "DCS 16.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tāmekāmeva kavayaḥ stuvanti ||",
       "translated_text": "Poets praise that style alone.",
       "segment_number": 360923
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.5",
      "label": "DCS 16.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sati raktari satyarthe sati śabdānuśāsane",
       "translated_text": "Even when a speaker, a subject, and command of language are present,",
       "segment_number": 360924
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "asti tatra vinā yena parikṣarati vāṅmadhu ||",
       "translated_text": "there is still something without which the honey of speech drains away.",
       "segment_number": 360925
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.6",
      "label": "DCS 16.6"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "udāharaṇam ||",
       "translated_text": "An example:",
       "segment_number": 360926
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_16.7",
      "label": "DCS 16.7"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "gāhantāṃ mahimā nipānasalilaṃ śṛṅgairmuhustāḍitaṃ chāyābaddhakadambakaṃ mṛgakulaṃ romanyam abhyasyatu",
       "translated_text": "Let the buffaloes plunge into the water of the drinking pool, repeatedly struck by their horns, and let the herd of deer gathered in the shade practice rumination.",
       "segment_number": 360927
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "viśrabdhaiḥ kriyatāṃ varāhapatibhirmustākṣatiḥ palvale viśrāmaṃ labhatāmidaṃ ca śithilajyābandhamasmaddhanuḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "Let the lordly boars confidently root up <s>mustā</s> plants in the marsh, and let this bow of ours, its bowstring loosened, find rest.",
       "segment_number": 360928
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "17"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 17"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_17.1",
      "label": "DCS 17.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ojaśca kāntiśca yasyāṃ staḥ seyamojaḥkāntimatī gauḍīyā nāma rītiḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "The style in which vigor and brilliance are present is called <s>Gauḍīyā</s>, possessing vigor and brilliance.",
       "segment_number": 360929
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_17.2",
      "label": "DCS 17.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "mādhuryasaukumāryayor abhāvāt sasamāsabahulātyantodbhaṭapadā ca ||",
       "translated_text": "Because sweetness and delicacy are absent, it abounds in compounds and contains exceedingly forceful words.",
       "segment_number": 360930
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_17.3",
      "label": "DCS 17.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "atra ślokaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "Here is a verse:",
       "segment_number": 360931
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
